Q: How to make a text clickable in Jetpack Compose? And also toggle it to non-clickable after selecting once A: <p>I think the easiest is to use the <code>.clickable</code> modifier.  Here's some sample code.  I use a mutable boolean to remember if the text has been clicked or not.  And there are two versions of the Text (one that is clickable, one that is not).</p>
<pre><code>var clicked by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }
if (clicked == false) {
    Text(
        modifier = Modifier.clickable {
            clicked = true
            onClick()
        }
        text = &quot;Resend OTP&quot;
    )
}
else {
    Text(text = &quot;Resend OTP&quot;)
}    

</code></pre>
<p>Pretty basic, no tricks.  But it works and is easy to understand.  And pretty easy to modify if you want different colors for the not-clickable version of the Text.</p>

Q: Changing git commit message after push (given that no one pulled from remote) A: <p>Below is also one of the ways by which it can be achieved.</p>
<pre><code>git reset --soft &lt;commit-id&gt;
git commit -m &quot;message&quot;
git push -f
</code></pre>
